OL,3,GNEWSADancer's family were told to say
OL,4,Agoodbye after stroke - now he hopes to
OL,5,Aperform again
OL,6,
OL,7,FAfter a dancer suffered a sudden
OL,8,Fstroke, doctors told his family to say
OL,9,Fgoodbye as there was nothing more they
OL,10,Fcould do.
OL,12,FDaniel Parsonage, 29, underwent two
OL,13,Femergency operations and spent four
OL,14,Fweeks in an induced coma in July last
OL,15,Fyear. Severe bleeding on the brain
OL,16,Fmeant his family feared the worst.
OL,18,FBut he pulled through and while it was
OL,19,Fbelieved he would never walk or talk
OL,20,Fagain, he has vowed to "keep fighting"
OL,21,Fto fully regain his speech and wants to
OL,22,Fbe performing again before he turns 30.
OL,23,APub: 26-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBWales NewsC Reg TVFClean Feed
FL,439,430,260,140,0,100
